            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 81-year-old female patient, admitted on 21/08/2006 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gases confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement of respiratory function. She was discharged on 22/08/2006 in stable condition. Please continue inhaled maintenance therapy and ensure close follow-up. Patient education regarding exacerbation recognition was provided prior to discharge. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
